From: rive
Subject: [PATCH 0048] add the rel32 addend COFF keeps in the field

COFF has no explicit addends, so LLVM leaves each IMAGE_REL_AMD64_REL32
addend in the field it relocates. The addend is -1 when an immediate byte
follows the displacement, as in cmpsd, blendpd and vblendvpd, and 4N where
function N reads its aot_stack_sizes slot. wamrc copies the field and emits
an addend of 0, and the Windows loader overwrote the field, so those float
constants were read one byte late and every stack check read the first
slot. The loader now adds the field, as its ADDR32 and ADDR64 cases already
do, so artifacts from earlier wamrcs load right.

--- a/core/iwasm/aot/arch/aot_reloc_x86_64.c
+++ b/core/iwasm/aot/arch/aot_reloc_x86_64.c
@@ -259,6 +259,9 @@
             }
 
 #if defined(BH_PLATFORM_WINDOWS)
+            /* COFF keeps the addend in the field, such as -1 when an
+               immediate byte follows the displacement. */
+            target_addr += *(int32 *)(target_section_addr + reloc_offset);
             target_addr -= sizeof(int32);
 #endif
             if ((int32)target_addr != target_addr) {
